  "worked_solution": "Notice that the function $q(x)$ is differentiable for all $x\\ne 1.$ Therefore, the correct answer is $q(x)={\\begin{aligned}x-1 & x<1 \\\\ x+1, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}.$\n\nAll other functions are not differentiable at $x=0.$\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $g(x)$ has a corner point at $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $p(x)$ has a vertical tangent at  $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.\n\n- The function $h(x)$ is not defined at $x=0$, so it is not differentiable there.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
